{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>until</b> — future in place of past, as if speaking of standing time, as I have explained." "And the meaning of <b>the sanctuaries of El</b> — that there are the priests of HaShem and the sages of Israel, and they revealed this sod, which is <i>to understand their latter end</i>, for man was not brought into this world to enjoy it or to be a king or wealthy, but only that his latter end be good, and this is the reward of the souls of the righteous."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:16.023672847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}